{
  "name": "When a prospect books a meeting, stop the sequence and update HubSpot",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## When a prospect books a meeting, stop the sequence and update HubSpot\n\n### How it works\nA booked meeting should end the sequence at once. The Calendly Trigger fires when an invitee books. The workflow searches the Argorant inbox for that email. If a conversation exists, it sets its status (meeting_booked by default; switch that status on in Argorant or use meeting_request) and removes the person from that campaign so no follow-up is sent. Either way, the contact is created or updated in HubSpot with the lifecycle stage sales qualified lead.\n\nNo credits are used.\n\n### Setup\n1. Install the community node **n8n-nodes-argorant** (tested with 0.3.0 on n8n 2.46.6): Settings > Community nodes > Install. Guide: https://github.com/argorant/n8n-nodes-argorant\n2. Add an **Argorant API** credential with a key from Argorant (Settings, API keys).\n3. Add a Calendly credential to **Meeting booked**.\n4. In **Settings**, keep status_key meeting_booked (switch it on in Argorant, Settings, Reply statuses) or use meeting_request.\n5. Add a HubSpot App Token credential (private app, contacts write) to **Update HubSpot** and activate.\n\n### Customization\nChange the lifecycle stage, or post the booking to your team chat as well.",
        "height": 609,
        "width": 520,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "7efa45ce-a9ed-4d94-a79c-9e64d8db1458",
      "name": "Overview",
